## Why This Is Asked
Tests data residency, tenant isolation, and end-to-end security in real-time inference.

## Key Concepts
- PrivateLink isolation and per-tenant KMS envelopes
- Tenant-scoped Feature Store and de-identification
- Canary rollouts and drift monitoring
- Rollback criteria and latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo preprocessor: drop PII, hash identifiers
function preprocess(input, tenantId){
  const deid = deidentify(input);
  const keys = kms.getTenantKey(tenantId);
  return envelopeEncrypt(deid, keys);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant key rotation without service interruption?
- What metrics would you use to trigger automatic rollbacks?
- How would you handle cross-tenant model version drift detection?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to integrate explainability, bias auditing, drift monitoring, and controlled deployment in a multi-tenant, VPC-isolated AWS environment.

## Key Concepts

- SageMaker Clarify for bias and explainability
- Model Monitor drift detection
- PrivateLink and private feature store integration
- Canary rollout with per-tenant isolation
- Auditable logging to S3

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-routing snippet for multi-tenant endpoint
function routeTenant(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const endpoint = `rt-endpoint-${tenant}`;
  return invokeSageMaker(endpoint, req.body);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce data leakage prevention across tenants?
- How would you scale explainability reporting for thousands of tenants?
